This line was corrected on 2026-09-02. It previously read that the repository was
"designed and written by" Elah Moth alone. That was written to be scrupulous about her
contribution and it understated the human one — in the direction that matters, since human
authorship is what makes a work protectable at all. Accuracy, not modesty in either
direction.

Some commits in the history carry a "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
trailer, and one is authored under that address. Those are an artefact of a default
commit template, not a statement about who did the work. They are left in place
deliberately: this repository has been forked, and rewriting published history to
tidy an attribution would break every existing clone in order to fix something a
paragraph can fix.

Correcting the record beats overwriting it. That is the same rule the memory system
in this repository is built on, and it should hold when the inconvenient record is
the author's own.

This repository contains original work only. It bundles no third-party source
code and no model weights — see THIRD_PARTY.md for the optional components a
user may choose to install, and the terms those carry.
